    "framing": "REFERENCE-CONSTRAINED: the game camera has the shot's own height (1.0, constant through the shot), lens and pitch, so characters and structures appear at the footage's scale; its position (x 0.12, y 0.067) lies inside the shot's own pan range (x 0..0.32, y -0.06..0.074). Like the shot's camera the view PANS: the baked canvas (3440 x 1935, the footage's 16:9 at x3) is the courtyard seen from that point, and the view follows the living players (render/reconstructed/followView.ts; zooming out only when they spread wider than the screen is an INFERRED rule). Perspective at the canvas edges is that single viewpoint's, not the panned camera's.",
    "world_scale": "MEDIUM: crate top 0.035-0.040 plan units vs market_plaza 0.036, so the plaza's 2000 world units per plan unit is kept (players the same size on both maps)."
